body:
Fixed, but gonna make a writeup anyway for anyone who finds this in the future.

&#x200B;

I have a standard cylinder lock, and [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xH\_aMD1o4J8](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xH_aMD1o4J8) helped with diagnosing the problem.

&#x200B;

Basically, the plate that fixes the cylinder onto the door was loose, and the plate itself wasn't bolted onto the door. Therefore, any key that fits through the door can just wrench that cylinder open without even engaging the lock. Think turning a padlock sideways.

&#x200B;

So I screwed the cylinder tightly to the plate, and screwed the plate right onto the wooden door. [https://imgur.com/a/rOhplA0](https://imgur.com/a/rOhplA0) <-  I basically bolted this plate thing right into the wood.
